<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victorinus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 271</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Marcus Piavonius Victorinus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victorinus was emperor of the breakaway <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallic-empire">Gallic Empire</a> from 269 to 271. A senior officer under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/postumus">Postumus</a>, he took power after the short reign of Marius and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> returned to the central empire. He was murdered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> in 271 by one of his officers, reportedly over a private grievance, and was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetricus-i">Tetricus I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victorinus.jpg" alt="Victorinus" width="292" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Omicroñ'R · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aureus_Victorinus_RIC_0094_(obverse).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
